            "review_title": "Review at Onvit",
            "review_text": "Andy\nTaipei, Taiwan388 contributions\n0\nVietnam's First Korean Star\nJul 2026 • Solo\nOnvit is the first Korean restaurant in Vietnam to earn a Michelin star. The dining room felt notably spacious right from the entrance. Among the openers, the Hanwoo bulgogi bite was the standout, layered with truffle and mushroom. Equally memorable was the abalone porridge, its soft rice set against crisp, chewy greens. The short loin arrived with an unexpectedly full spread of banchan. The seasoning was bold and homestyle, and it will not suit everyone. Not everything landed, though. The beef tongue tteokgalbi lacked the fattiness the cut should have. The Spanish mackerel sauce was quite salty, but the mugwort puree balanced the brine. Even the pear sorbet finished on a heavy note of ginger. I would consider a return visit once the menu changes.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten July 25, 2026",
